name: "eval"
type: "module"
about: "
Tree-walking evaluator for AiR ASTs.

Imports prelude to build LOOKUP — the global function/operator table.
No circular dependency: eval → prelude, not the other way.

Entry points:
  interpret(ast, env)         → evaluate a single AST node
  interpret_program(ast, env) → evaluate a full program (top-level bindings persist)
  eval_table(table, env)      → evaluate a TableNode as a code block

Special forms (detected by key presence in table.map):
  { if: cond, then: expr, else: expr }               — conditional
  { init: {...}, cond: expr, loop: {...} }            — loop with state
  (define key value)                                  — bind in current env
  (eval table)                                        — explicitly evaluate lazy table

Evaluation model:
  Numbers, Strings, Symbols  → unwrapped Python values
  TableNode                  → lazy (returned as-is)
  IdentifierNode             → env chain lookup, then LOOKUP
  EvalNode (<: expr)         → force-evaluate a table

Future backends (same interface, different implementation):
  bytecode    — compile to stack-machine bytecode, run on a VM
  compile_py  — emit Python source from AST
"
